      "description": "Basketball Table Crew Salary $20.00 Hourly Location St. Bonaventure, NY Job Type Temporary Job Number 202200645 Division Athletics Department Athletics Opening Date 09/22/2026 Description Benefits Description Work St. Bonaventure home men’s and women’s basketball games, as well as other non-St. Bonaventure basketball games by performing duties such as Time Out Coordinator, Game Clock Operator, Scoreboard Operator, Shot Clock Operator, Official Scorer, Public Address Announcer, and Official Statistician. Examples of Duties Support the operation of the basketball game and the basketball officials by performing a table crew role. 100% Supplemental Functions: Other duties as assigned Typical Qualifications Education: None Years of Experience: None Working Conditions / Physical Requirements: Must be able to sit for at least an hour at a time. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Other Perks Free access to campus fitness center Other National and Local discounts available St. Bonaventure University is located in the scenic Enchanted Mountain region of Western New York, approximately 75 miles south of Buffalo, New York, with easy access to major metropolitan areas. A close-knit and caring community guided by its values of compassion, wisdom and integrity, St. Bonaventure is dedicated to academic excellence as informed by its Franciscan and liberal arts traditions. The university is committed to developing an inclusive community and preparing leaders dedicated to ethical conduct and compassionate service. The university currently enrolls approximately 2,000 undergraduate students and more than 1,000 graduate students in its schools of Arts and Sciences, Business, Education, Communication, and Health Professions. U.S. News & World Report ranks SBU in the top 15% of regional universities in the North, for both value and overall. St. Bonaventure is a member of the Atlantic 10 Conference (NCAA D