      "title": "Level 2 PC/LAN Technician",
      "description": "Level 2 PC/LAN Technician Salary $24.23 - $29.23 Hourly Location St. Bonaventure, NY Job Type Full Time Job Number 202200655 Division Academic Affairs Department Technology Services Opening Date 10/27/2026 Description Benefits Description The Level 2 technician provides advanced technical support and takes responsibility for daily tasks assigned to the help desk. The technician resolves complex support issues while completing projects assigned by the Director of User Services. The primary role for this position will oversee imaging and support for all campus computers and will directly oversee setup and support for all labs, classroom and student lounge systems. Applicant must have a strong working knowledge of Microsoft Intune, Entra and SCCM. In addition to these daily duties, the technician assists the Network Services Manager with a broad range of network management functions, including print management for employees and students. Examples of Duties Oversee imaging setup and support for all campus computers. Directly oversee setup and support for all labs, classroom and student lounge systems. 30% Assist the Director of Technology Infrastructure and Security with implementing and supporting various network management services, including Group Policy, print management, and Active Directory services. 30% Provide advanced technical assistance to faculty, students, and administrators. 10% Communicate proactively with the User Services Manager and provide the front-line perspective needed to implement improvements or changes. 10% Diagnose and repair software and hardware problems for PCs and Macs. 10% Troubleshoot and resolve user account issues 5% Log help desk calls completely and accurately in the ticket-tracking system, including all pertinent end-user identification information and a detailed description of the problem. 3% Contribute to the development and documentation of procedures, and cross-train other help desk technicians on hardware and software installation, general troubleshooting, service, repair, and maintenance. 2% Typical Qualifications Bachelors Degree preferred. Minimum of associate degree in computer science or a related field is required Minimum of five (5) years technical background with computer experience. Network and server experience preferred. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of principles of PC and Macintosh use and operation. Knowledge of Office Applications, Windows/Mac operating systems, and various pc peripheral devices such as scanners, digital cameras, printers. Knowledge of LANs/WANs and server setup/maintenance Knowledge of Microsoft Intune, Entra, Azure and SCCM Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with University employees and the community. Working Conditions and Physical Requirements Ability to lift and transport computer equipment weighing approximately 40 pounds. Full-time employees at SBU enjoy unparalleled Benefits Abundance of Time off Tuition Remission 100% undergraduate tuition remission for employee, spouse, and dependents 80% graduate tuition remission for employee (online and ground programs) 50% for spouse (ground programs only) Full Benefit package 403b Retirement Plan + 10% Employer contribution after 2 years Health Insurance with $250 Wellness card Dental Insurance Employer Paid Life insurance Short-term Disability Employer Paid Long-term Disability Employee Assistance Program Other Perks Free access to campus fitness center 2 free Division 1 Men’s & Women's Basketball Season tickets Golf course membership discount Other National and Local discounts available St. Bonaventure University is located in the scenic Enchanted Mountain region of Western New York, approximately 75 miles south of Buffalo, New York, with easy access to major metropolitan areas. A close-knit and caring community guided by its values of compassion, wisdom and integrity, St. Bonaventure is dedicated to academic excellence as informed by its Franciscan and liberal arts traditions. The university is committed to developing an inclusive community and preparing leaders dedicated to ethical conduct and compassionate service. The university currently enrolls approximately 2,000 undergraduate students and more than 1,000 graduate students in its schools of Arts and Sciences, Business, Education, Communication, and Health Professions. U.S. News & World Report ranks SBU in the top 15% of regional universities in the North, for both value and overall. St. Bonaventure is a member of the Atlantic 10 Conference (NCAA Division I), with athletes participating in 20 sports. St. Bonaventure University is committed to providing a comprehensive benefits program designed to attract and retain high-quality Faculty and Staff. To view an overview of the benefits offered at SBU for full time employees, click the link below: Benefits Overview for Full-Time Employees Employer St. Bonaventure University (NY) Address 3261 West State Road St. Bonaventure, New York, 14778 Website http://www.sbu.edu Apply"
